{"id":"importlib.machinery/NamespacePath","module":"importlib.machinery","qualname":"NamespacePath","name":"NamespacePath","kind":"class","parent":null,"signatures":["NamespacePath(name, path, path_finder)"],"doc":"Represents a namespace package's path.\n\nIt uses the module *name* to find its parent module, and from there it looks\nup the parent's __path__. When this changes, the module's own path is\nrecomputed, using *path_finder*. The initial value is set to *path*.\n\nFor top-level modules, the parent module's path is sys.path.\n\n*path_finder* should be a callable with the same signature as\nMetaPathFinder.find_spec((fullname, path, target=None) -> spec).","docsUrl":"https://docs.python.org/3.15/library/importlib.html#importlib.machinery.NamespacePath","added":"3.15","changed":[],"deprecated":null,"availability":[],"source":{"path":"Lib/importlib/_bootstrap_external.py","line":1061},"implDetail":false,"isAsync":false},
